                       Extract
                       =======


Utility to extract a description for certain file-types
Anti-Copyright (A) 2002 Markus Schwab <g17m0@lycos.com>
-----------------------------------------------------------------------


At the moment only the following documents are supported (identified according
to the extension - so don't cheat ;) ):

  - JPEG: Extracts the properties according two styles; either one simple
 	  comment (as written by e.g. The GIMP) or a more complex versions
	  (as created by Windows XP or - even more complex - PhotoShop).
  - HTML: The text in between <title> and </title> and/or the contents of
	  the meta tags (supported are the tags according HTML 4.0 and
	  Dublin Core) is extracted.
  - PDF: The content of the "document information dictionary" is extracted
         Note that the content of the "Subject" key is returned as comment!
  - StarOffice documents (*.sdw, *.sdc, *.sdd, *.sda); the comments of the
          properties dialog is extracted
  - MS office documents (*.doc, *.xls, *.ppt); the comment of the properties
	  dialog is extracted.

The found results can be written either in text, HTML (table) or LaTeX
(tabular) format. Note that there is no extra formatting of the text (like
checking for LaTeX or HTML special characters) or special formatting of the
output.


Installation
------------

See the file INSTALL


Windows
-------

Is supported (principally), though because of missing standards not that easy
(at least, if you have a different setup than me). See the (end of the) file
INSTALL. Note that the General library is linked statically (and not used as
a DLL).


How to report bugs and/or send patches
--------------------------------------

Bug reports and patches should be send to the e-mail address of the author
(g17m0@lycos). Feel free to also send comments.

If you report a bug, please be sure to add anything which might be of use! Like

  - The version of the utility.
  - The version of the used General library.
  - How to reproduce the bug; a file provocing it would be great.
  - In case of a crash there should also be a stackdump in your systemlog which
    might help in localizing the bug.
  - Anything else you think might be helpful.
